<section><h2 class="ref-sec-title">Events</h2><ol class="day-events yr-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-6">6 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">The Abbasids execute the 42 captives of Amorium at Samarra</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasids</a> executed at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/samarra">Samarra</a> 42 Byzantine officers and notables, taken hostage in the sack of Amorium in 838, after they refused to convert to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/islam">Islam</a>. Repeated Byzantine efforts to ransom them had been rebuffed.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abbasid-caliphate">Abbasid Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/vikings" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/vikings.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/march-29">29 March</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Viking raiders plunder Paris and hold it for ransom</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">A <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Viking</a> fleet of 120 ships under the Norse chieftain Reginherus, or Ragnar, sailed up the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/seine">Seine</a> and plundered and occupied <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/paris">Paris</a>, holding it for a large ransom. Reginherus has been tentatively identified with the legendary Ragnar Lodbrok.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vikings">Vikings</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb"><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/today-in-history/november-22">22 November</a></p><h3 class="tih-event-title">Nominoe's Bretons defeat Charles the Bald at Ballon</h3><p class="tih-event-desc">The Breton ruler <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nominoe">Nominoe</a> defeated the West Frankish king <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a> at Ballon, near Bains-sur-Oust in eastern Brittany. Charles was forced to accept Nominoe's authority in Brittany, a key step towards an independent Breton kingdom.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ballon">Battle of Ballon</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/charles-the-bald">Charles the Bald</a></div></div></li></ol></section>
